{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "23", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "53", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "Wonder Cement & Dalmia Bharat's limestone mining projects near Rajasthan's Great Indian Bustard 'priority area' approved", "para": "Rajasthan's Jaisalmer region has given the green light to two limestone mining initiatives that encounter the habitats of the Great Indian Bustard. One project intrudes on a designated priority area, while the other lies a kilometer away. Despite concerns over the longevity of endangered species conservation, these projects were approved, with environmental assessments indicating minor impacts and the need for ongoing monitoring and protective measures.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/wonder-cement-dalmia-bharats-limestone-mining-projects-near-rajasthans-great-indian-bustard-priority-area-approved/135134572?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-2098358/135134572.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}, {"title": "Lucknow development body plans levy charge to fund pending works in Sushant Golf City", "para": "In Sushant Golf City, property owners may face a new completion charge tied to building approvals. This fee is intended to support ongoing infrastructure projects, covering crucial developments like roadways and sewage systems. However, plot holders of EWS and LIG with smaller plots will be exempt, benefitting more than 10,000 allottees. The Lucknow Development Authority aims to enhance the completion procedure to better manage the township's future.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/lucknow-development-body-plans-levy-charge-to-fund-pending-works-in-sushant-golf-city/135134335?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-116434/135134335.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Property fraud cases rise in South Goa despite SIT probe", "para": "South Goa is witnessing a surge in land-grab activities and property fraud. The police have taken action by registering several FIRs against these criminal acts. Notably, one complaint revolves around false claims of land ownership and suspicious contracts between involved parties. Additionally, there\u2019s a case of property being improperly used as collateral for a hefty bank loan.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/property-fraud-cases-rise-in-south-goa-despite-sit-probe/135134219?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-120298/135134219.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}